In this game, players take turns rolling a standard six-sided die. Each player starts with a score of 0, and on each turn, they add the value of their roll to their score. However, if a player rolls a 1, their score is reset to 0 and it becomes the next player's turn. The first player to reach a score of 20 or more wins.
Additionally, the program should allow the user to input the number of players and automatically run through the game until a winner is declared. It should also print out the scores after each turn.
